using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Globalization;
using System.Text;
using PoliSim.Data;
using PoliSim.Data.Generated;
using PoliSim.Simulation;
using UnityEngine;

namespace PoliSim.EditorTools
{
    /// <summary>
    /// K276 (Elias, 2026-10-29, answering K245): <b>labour-force participation rises by cohort and with statutory pension ages, sourced from the EC
    /// Ageing Report 2024 and CBO.</b> It fails while the statement is false. Every sourced figure is read from ParticipationPath (generated by
    /// Tools/k276_participation_prep.pl) and every expected figure is this file's own recomputation from it, never the model's.
    /// <list type="number">
    /// <item><b>(a) The cohort rates ARE the sources' paths.</b> For the six countries at the stated years (the EU five 2030, 2040, 2050, 2070; the USA
    /// 2030, 2040, 2055, 2099), every band's rate the model reads (ParticipationRateTable.RatesAt) equals the seed's sourced rate plus the change its
    /// source projects for the band's group since the base year (2024; the USA 2025), within RateTolerance, recomputed here from the age groups' own
    /// limits - the USA's groups weighted by the years each shares with the band, its sexes equally (DECLARED in ParticipationCohortPath). A band no
    /// group covers holds the seed's. (a2) The base year reads the seed's table; a year before the source's first reads the first year's change, a year
    /// after its last the last year's.</item>
    /// <item><b>(b) The pension age moves the older cohorts by the sourced response, and the player's statute is the input.</b> On a seeded world, per
    /// country, at 2030 and 2045, the response measured from the REFERENCE - the age the projection was made under: the statute's for the year, or past
    /// an indexed statute's horizon (Sweden after 2032, Italy after 2028) the Ageing Report's country fiche's age, linear between its years and never
    /// below the carried figure, recomputed here from the generated fiche arrays (review 1, M1; the prereg's r2-1/r2-2): (b1) with no bill the response
    /// is this file's recomputation of the response from the reference to the statute's figure - exactly zero, and the structural rate the pyramid's at
    /// the year's projected rates bit for bit, where the two agree; negative past an indexed horizon; (b2) a bill passed through the game's own step
    /// (ParliamentSystem.ApplyBillResult) setting the age a year above the statute's becomes the age in force and moves participation by this file's
    /// recomputation of the response from the reference to the bill's figure - Σ band × the share of the band between the two ages × the step (the
    /// country's measured effect, else the year's projected rate a year below the lower age × the median hazard 0.425; Atav, Jongen &amp; Rabaté 2021,
    /// Table B.1), each band capped at its room - all of it in the bands at 55 and over, its sign that of (the bill - the reference); (b3) a year below,
    /// the same; (b4) a bill returning the statute's figure returns the response to its (b1) value.</item>
    /// <item><b>(c) The labour force against the sources, the no-policy run</b> (the six centuries, NoPolicyCentury), as an index on the first year of the
    /// run the source covers: the EU five's OWN labour force aged 20-74 on the law the source projects (NoPolicyCentury.LabourForce2074At: the state's
    /// rate over the structural rate × the active people aged 20-74 at the year's projected rates - it reads the state, and it carries 65-74; review 1,
    /// M2, the prereg's r2-3) within LabourForceBand of the Ageing Report's labour force aged 20-74 (table II.1.53's employment / (1 - II.1.51's
    /// unemployment rate)) at 2030, 2040, 2050 and 2070 - the 20-64 construct against II.1.26 printed beside it as information; the USA's labour force
    /// (15+ at the state's rate) against CBO's potential labor force (LTBO, March 2025, compounded from its growth rates) at 2030, 2040 and 2055. Every
    /// year is the pyramid's own (K299's amendment r2, the review's M2: NoPolicyCentury.Year.SubstrateYear, as (d) reads it).
    /// K290: a (c) line in <see cref="RegisteredLabourForce"/> prints a named REGISTERED MISS and does not fail while its attribution holds (the K218
    /// pattern); the rule and the band are unchanged, a registered line that holds says the registration can be lifted, and a miss whose attribution no
    /// longer holds FAILS. K313 (fisc2, 2026-10-30): Poland 2050 is registered on K290's mechanism with its own attribution - the line with the health and
    /// education participation terms removed inside the band, and their part at most a point (<see cref="RegisteredHealthEducationPartBound"/>).</item>
    /// <item><b>(d) K299 (K290's follow-up): the USA's population against CBO's 2025 demographics</b> (UsDemographicOutlook, Tools/uspop_prep.pl), the
    /// no-policy run, by the pyramid's own year, an index on 2025, at 2030, 2040 and 2055 (the path is CBO's by-age table, band by band - K299's
    /// amendment r3): (d1) each of the four Figure 2 age groups and the sum from 25 within UsGroupBand of CBO's index, the whole population printed
    /// against CBO's total; (d2) the 16+ within UsCivilianBand of CBO's civilian noninstitutionalized 16+ (Figure 10); (d3) the 15+ and the 16+ within
    /// UsAdultBand of CBO's own (the table's single years). The bands are K299's prereg and its amendment r3 (Reviews/2026-10-29_uspop_prereg.md),
    /// DECLARED before any run of the tree they govern.</item>
    /// </list>
    /// The bands and years are K276's prereg (Reviews/2026-10-29_k276_prereg.md), DECLARED before any run; its amendment r2 re-forms (b) and the EU's (c)
    /// after review 1, before any run of the amended tree. Prints `PARTICIPATION COHORTS: PASS` and exits 0
    /// when every check holds; each failure is a `PARTICIPATION COHORTS: FAIL` error naming its check, each registered miss a
    /// `PARTICIPATION COHORTS: REGISTERED MISS` line.
    /// Run: `Unity.exe -batchmode -nographics -projectPath &lt;path&gt; -executeMethod PoliSim.EditorTools.ParticipationCohortDiagnostic.Run -logFile &lt;path&gt;`.
    /// </summary>
    public static class ParticipationCohortDiagnostic
    {
        /// <summary>[AUTHORED] a band's rate against this file's recomputation, as a fraction - float's step near 1 is 6e-8, and the model sums a float
        /// change onto a float seed where this file works in double.</summary>
        private const double RateTolerance = 1e-6;

        /// <summary>[AUTHORED] the response against this file's recomputation, relative - one float sum over twenty bands.</summary>
        private const double ResponseTolerance = 1e-4;

        /// <summary>[AUTHORED] the band on the labour force's index against the source's index, a share - DECLARED before any run (K276's prereg).</summary>
        private const double LabourForceBand = 0.03;

        /// <summary>The stated years of (a) and (c).</summary>
        private static readonly int[] EuYears = { 2030, 2040, 2050, 2070 };
        private static readonly int[] UsRateYears = { 2030, 2040, 2055, 2099 };
        private static readonly int[] UsLabourYears = { 2030, 2040, 2055 };

        /// <summary>The years (b) passes its bills in.</summary>
        private static readonly int[] BillYears = { 2030, 2045 };

        /// <summary>The Ageing Report's four groups: first age, last age, the series.</summary>
        private static readonly (int Lo, int Hi, string Name)[] EuGroups = { (20, 24, "young 20-24 (II.1.29)"), (25, 54, "prime-age 25-54 (II.1.30)"), (55, 64, "older 55-64 (II.1.31)"), (65, 74, "oldest 65-74 (II.1.32)") };

        private static readonly CountryId[] Six = { CountryId.Sweden, CountryId.Germany, CountryId.France, CountryId.Italy, CountryId.Poland, CountryId.USA };

        /// <summary>
        /// K290 (the integrator under Elias's standing instruction, 2026-10-29; review 2's M1): THE (c) LINES REGISTERED AS MISSES, keyed "Country year",
        /// each with its attribution. A registered line prints a REGISTERED MISS and does not fail ONLY while the attribution holds: for the USA, the
        /// population part of the miss (the model's 15+ population index against the population CBO's all-people rate applies to) lies within
        /// <see cref="RegisteredPopulationTolerance"/> of the part MEASURED when the line was registered, while the rate part (the model's labour force over
        /// its 15+ population, against CBO's all-people rate) is inside the band. Review 3 (L1): the registration has a ceiling as well as a floor, so a
        /// later regression in the population - a miss growing past what was measured and attributed - FAILS instead of printing as the registered miss.
        /// A registered line whose attribution stops holding is asserted and FAILS; one that holds says so, so the registration can be lifted.
        /// <para>K299 (K290's follow-up): K290's one line, USA 2040, was lifted when the US population was recalibrated on CBO's 2025 demographics and
        /// the line printed that its registration could be lifted (the record names the run); the mechanism stayed for a later registration, which a ruling
        /// names.</para>
        /// <para>K313 (fisc2, 2026-10-30; the prereg's amendment 2, written after the measurement): POLAND 2050, attributed to the health and education terms -
        /// K222's declared M1 drift (the health and education lines at the going wage read as capacity), which K269 (a)'s R1 brings into the player's book. It
        /// stays registered only while the line with those two terms removed from the state's rate (at the year and at the base year) is inside the band AND
        /// their part - the line less that line - is at most <see cref="RegisteredHealthEducationPartBound"/>. The mortality route through the 15+ population
        /// cannot be separated from the run's own pyramid, so it stays inside the line without the terms and is not bounded by the second test.</para>
        /// </summary>
        private static readonly Dictionary<string, (string Tag, string Reason, Attribution Kind, double MeasuredPopulationPart)> RegisteredLabourForce = new Dictionary<string, (string, string, Attribution, double)>
        {
            { "Poland 2050", ("K313", "the health and education participation terms of K222's declared M1 drift, in the player's book since K269 (a)", Attribution.HealthEducationPart, double.NaN) },
        };

        /// <summary>K290 / K313: what a registered (c) line's attribution reads - K290's population part against CBO's (the USA), or K313's health and education
        /// terms (an EU country).</summary>
        private enum Attribution { PopulationPart, HealthEducationPart }

        /// <summary>K313: [AUTHORED-DRAFT] the most of a registered line's miss the health and education terms may carry, a share (one point; measured at the
        /// ruling about a third of it).</summary>
        private const double RegisteredHealthEducationPartBound = 0.01;

        /// <summary>[AUTHORED] review 3 (L1): how far a registered line's population part may lie from the part measured at its registration, a share (one
        /// point either way) - wide enough for the run-to-run and runtime rounding of the printed tenth, narrow enough that a population regression of
        /// a point or more fails rather than hides under the registration.</summary>
        private const double RegisteredPopulationTolerance = 0.01;

        private static int _failures;
        private static int _registered;
        private static StringBuilder _sb;

        public static void Run()
        {
            CheckExit.ArmLogFold();
            _failures = 0; _registered = 0;
            _sb = new StringBuilder("PARTICIPATION COHORTS: K276 - the rates by age along the Ageing Report 2024's and CBO's paths, the pension age's response with the player's statute as its input, the labour force against the sources (seed 777)\n");
            try
            {
                Rates();
                Response();
                LabourForce();
                Population();   // K299
            }
            catch (Exception e) { Check(false, "the run threw " + e.GetType().Name + ": " + e.Message + "\n" + e.StackTrace); }
            Debug.Log(_sb.ToString());
            if (_registered > 0) { Debug.Log(F("PARTICIPATION COHORTS: {0} REGISTERED MISS line(s) (K290's mechanism - K313: Poland 2050 - printed, not failed, each with its attribution holding)", _registered)); }
            Debug.Log(_failures == 0
                ? "PARTICIPATION COHORTS: PASS - every band's rate is its seed plus its source's projected change at the stated years, the response measures from the age the projection was made under (zero on the statute's own path, the carried statute's shortfall past an indexed horizon), a bill's age moves the older cohorts by the sourced response, the labour force holds the sources' index within the band but the line K313 registers (printed above), and the USA's population holds CBO's 2025 demographics within K299's bands"
                : F("PARTICIPATION COHORTS: FAIL - {0} check(s) failed.", _failures));
            CheckExit.Finish(_failures == 0 ? 0 : 1);
        }

        // ============================================================ (a) the cohort rates
        private static void Rates()
        {
            _sb.Append(F("    a. the rates by age against the sources (the EU five's base {0}, the USA's {1}; tolerance {2:E0})\n", ParticipationCohortPath.EuBaseYear, ParticipationCohortPath.UsBaseYear, RateTolerance));
            foreach (CountryId id in Six)
            {
                float[] seed = ParticipationRateTable.For(id);
                Check(seed != null && ParticipationCohortPath.Has(id), F("(a) {0,-8} carries a seed table and a sourced path", id));
                if (seed == null) { continue; }
                bool usa = id == CountryId.USA;
                int baseYear = usa ? ParticipationCohortPath.UsBaseYear : ParticipationCohortPath.EuBaseYear;
                int first = usa ? ParticipationPath.UsFirstYear : ParticipationPath.EuFirstYear;
                int last = usa ? ParticipationPath.UsLastYear : ParticipationPath.EuLastYear;
                // (a2) the base year reads the seed; before the first and after the last the path holds
                Check(Same(ParticipationRateTable.RatesAt(id, baseYear), seed), F("(a2) {0,-8} {1}, the base year, reads the seed's table", id, baseYear));
                Check(Same(ParticipationRateTable.RatesAt(id, first - 3), ParticipationRateTable.RatesAt(id, Math.Min(first, baseYear))) || usa && Same(ParticipationRateTable.RatesAt(id, first - 3), seed),
                    F("(a2) {0,-8} {1} reads {2}'s rates (the path held before its first year)", id, first - 3, usa ? baseYear : first));
                Check(Same(ParticipationRateTable.RatesAt(id, last + 10), ParticipationRateTable.RatesAt(id, last)), F("(a2) {0,-8} {1} reads {2}'s rates (held after the last year)", id, last + 10, last));

                foreach (int y in usa ? UsRateYears : EuYears)
                {
                    float[] model = ParticipationRateTable.RatesAt(id, y);
                    double worst = 0; int worstBand = -1, covered = 0;
                    for (int b = 0; b < PopulationCohorts.CohortCount; b++)
                    {
                        double change = usa ? UsChange(b, y) : EuChange(id, b, y, out bool _);
                        double expected = Math.Max(0.0, Math.Min(1.0, seed[b] + change / 100.0));
                        double d = Math.Abs(model[b] - expected);
                        if (d > worst) { worst = d; worstBand = b; }
                        if (change != 0.0) { covered++; }
                    }
                    Check(worst <= RateTolerance && covered > 0, F("(a) {0,-8} {1}: every band is its seed plus its source's change since {2} - worst {3:E1} (band {4}), {5} band(s) moved",
                        id, y, baseYear, worst, worstBand < 0 ? "-" : Band(worstBand), covered));
                    // the group's rate on the seed's pyramid, printed beside the source's level and change
                    var line = new StringBuilder();
                    if (usa)
                    {
                        foreach (int b in new[] { 4, 8, 11, 12, 13, 14 }) { line.Append(F(" {0} {1:F1} ({2:+0.0;-0.0})", Band(b), 100.0 * model[b], 100.0 * (model[b] - seed[b]))); }
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        foreach ((int lo, int hi, string name) in EuGroups)
                        {
                            Dictionary<CountryId, float[]> g = Group(lo);
                            line.Append(F(" {0} {1:F1} ({2:+0.0;-0.0})", name.Substring(0, name.IndexOf(' ')), At(g, id, y), At(g, id, y) - At(g, id, baseYear)));
                        }
                    }
                    _sb.Append(F("        info {0,-8} {1}: {2}{3}\n", id, y, usa ? "the model's bands, both sexes (change since 2025):" : "the source's groups (change since 2024):", line));
                }
            }
        }

        /// <summary>The Ageing Report's change for band b, points, from the base to the year; false in <paramref name="covered"/> where no group covers the band.</summary>
        private static double EuChange(CountryId id, int b, int year, out bool covered)
        {
            int lo = b * PopulationCohorts.CohortWidth, hi = lo + PopulationCohorts.CohortWidth - 1;
            foreach ((int glo, int ghi, string _) in EuGroups)
            {
                if (lo >= glo && hi <= ghi) { covered = true; Dictionary<CountryId, float[]> g = Group(glo); return (double)At(g, id, year) - At(g, id, ParticipationCohortPath.EuBaseYear); }
            }
            covered = false;
            return 0.0;
        }

        /// <summary>The Ageing Report's series for the group opening at <paramref name="lo"/>.</summary>
        private static Dictionary<CountryId, float[]> Group(int lo)
            => lo == 20 ? ParticipationPath.Young : lo == 25 ? ParticipationPath.Prime : lo == 55 ? ParticipationPath.Older : ParticipationPath.Oldest;

        /// <summary>A group's series value for a country at a year, held before the first and after the last.</summary>
        private static float At(Dictionary<CountryId, float[]> g, CountryId id, int year)
        {
            float[] s = g[id];
            return s[Math.Max(0, Math.Min(s.Length - 1, year - ParticipationPath.EuFirstYear))];
        }

        /// <summary>CBO's change for band b, points, from 2025 to the year: each CBO group weighted by the years it shares with the band (16-89 only), the
        /// sexes equally; zero before 2025 and for a band no group reaches.</summary>
        private static double UsChange(int b, int year)
        {
            if (year < ParticipationPath.UsFirstYear) { return 0.0; }
            int lo = b * PopulationCohorts.CohortWidth, hi = lo + PopulationCohorts.CohortWidth - 1;
            double sum = 0; int years = 0;
            for (int k = 0; k < ParticipationPath.UsGroups.Length; k++)
            {
                int glo = ParticipationPath.UsGroups[k][0], ghi = ParticipationPath.UsGroups[k][1];
                int overlap = Math.Min(hi, ghi) - Math.Max(lo, glo) + 1;
                if (overlap <= 0) { continue; }
                double m = UsAt(ParticipationPath.UsMale[k], year) - UsAt(ParticipationPath.UsMale[k], ParticipationPath.UsFirstYear);
                double f = UsAt(ParticipationPath.UsFemale[k], year) - UsAt(ParticipationPath.UsFemale[k], ParticipationPath.UsFirstYear);
                sum += overlap * 0.5 * (m + f); years += overlap;
            }
            return years > 0 ? sum / years : 0.0;
        }

        private static float UsAt(float[] s, int year) => s[Math.Max(0, Math.Min(s.Length - 1, year - ParticipationPath.UsFirstYear))];

        private static bool Same(float[] a, float[] b)
        {
            if (a == null || b == null || a.Length != b.Length) { return false; }
            for (int i = 0; i < a.Length; i++) { if (Math.Abs(a[i] - b[i]) > RateTolerance) { return false; } }
            return true;
        }

        private static string Band(int b) => b == PopulationCohorts.OpenBandIndex ? "100+" : F("{0}-{1}", b * 5, b * 5 + 4);

        // ============================================================ (b) the pension age's response, the player's statute as its input
        private static void Response()
        {
            _sb.Append("    b. the pension age's response from the age the projection was made under: zero on the statute's own path, the carried statute's shortfall past an indexed horizon; a bill's age moves the older cohorts by the sourced step\n");
            foreach (CountryId id in Six)
            {
                SimulationRandom.Seed(777);
                EnergyMarket.ResetCalibration();
                World world = WorldFactory.CreateDefault();
                Country c = world.GetCountry(id);
                if (!Check(c?.Cohorts != null && PensionAgeStatute.Has(id), F("(b) {0,-8} carries a pyramid and a statute", id))) { continue; }
                foreach (int y in BillYears)
                {
                    c.CalendarYear = y;
                    c.PensionAgeOverride = -1f;
                    float statute = PensionAgeStatute.AgeInForce(id, y);
                    double reference = ReferenceOwn(id, y);
                    float pyramid = ParticipationRateTable.StructuralRate(id, c.Cohorts.Counts, y);
                    // (b1) no bill: the response from the reference to the statute's figure - zero where they agree (the statute's own path is inside the
                    // sources' paths), the carried statute's shortfall past an indexed horizon (review 1, M1)
                    double noBill = ExpectedPoints(c, y, reference, statute, out double noBillOlder);
                    float points0 = ParticipationRateTable.PensionResponsePoints(c);
                    float structural0 = ParticipationRateTable.StructuralRate(c);
                    bool agree = Math.Abs(statute - reference) < 1e-4;
                    Check(agree ? points0 == 0f && structural0 == pyramid
                                : points0 < 0f && Math.Abs(points0 - noBill) <= ResponseTolerance * Math.Max(1e-3, Math.Abs(noBill)) && Math.Abs(noBillOlder - noBill) <= ResponseTolerance * Math.Max(1e-3, Math.Abs(noBill)),
                        F("(b1) {0,-8} {1}: with no bill (the statute's {2}; the reference {3:F3}{4}) the response is {5:+0.0000;-0.0000;0} pts against this file's {6:+0.0000;-0.0000;0}{7}; structural {8:F3} against the pyramid's at {1}'s rates {9:F3}",
                            id, y, PensionAgeStatute.Format(statute), reference, agree ? ", the statute's own" : ", the Ageing Report's past the statute's horizon", points0, noBill,
                            agree ? " - zero, the statute's own path inside the sources' paths" : " - the carried statute's shortfall, all of it at 55 and over", structural0, pyramid));

                    foreach (float delta in new[] { 1f, -1f })
                    {
                        float set = Mathf.Clamp(statute + delta, BudgetBill.PensionAgeMin, BudgetBill.PensionAgeMax);
                        var bill = new BudgetBill { PensionAgeSet = true, PensionAge = set };
                        ParliamentSystem.ApplyBillResult(c, bill, true, (x, z) => { }, y);
                        bool inForce = PensionAgeStatute.AgeInForce(c, y) == set;
                        double expected = ExpectedPoints(c, y, reference, set, out double older);
                        float points = ParticipationRateTable.PensionResponsePoints(c);
                        float structural = ParticipationRateTable.StructuralRate(c);
                        double d = set - reference;
                        bool signOk = Math.Abs(d) < 1e-4 ? points == 0f : d > 0 ? points > 0f && structural > pyramid : points < 0f && structural < pyramid;
                        Check(inForce && signOk && Math.Abs(points - expected) <= ResponseTolerance * Math.Max(1e-3, Math.Abs(expected)) && Math.Abs(older - expected) <= ResponseTolerance * Math.Max(1e-3, Math.Abs(expected)),
                            F("(b{0}) {1,-8} {2}: a bill setting {3} (the statute's {4}, the reference {5:F3}) is the age in force and moves the 15+ rate {6:+0.0000;-0.0000;0} pts against this file's {7:+0.0000;-0.0000;0}, all of it at 55 and over ({8:+0.0000;-0.0000;0}); structural {9:F3} against {10:F3}",
                                delta > 0f ? "2" : "3", id, y, PensionAgeStatute.Format(set), PensionAgeStatute.Format(statute), reference, points, expected, older, structural, pyramid));
                    }
                    // (b4) a bill returning the statute's figure
                    ParliamentSystem.ApplyBillResult(c, new BudgetBill { PensionAgeSet = true, PensionAge = -1f }, true, (x, z) => { }, y);
                    Check(c.PensionAgeOverride < 0f && ParticipationRateTable.PensionResponsePoints(c) == points0, F("(b4) {0,-8} {1}: a bill returning the statute's figure returns the response to its (b1) value ({2:+0.0000;-0.0000;0} pts)", id, y, points0));
                }
            }
        }

        /// <summary>This file's own reference (review 1, M1): the statute's age for the year inside its horizon and for a scheduled or fixed statute; past an
        /// indexed statute's horizon the Ageing Report's country-fiche age (ParticipationPath.ProjectedPensionAge), linear between the fiche's years, held
        /// before its first and after its last, and never below the statute's carried figure - recomputed here in double, not read from the model.</summary>
        private static double ReferenceOwn(CountryId id, int year)
        {
            double statute = PensionAgeStatute.AgeInForce(id, year);
            PensionAgeStatute.Rule rule = PensionAgeStatute.Of(id);
            if (rule == null || year <= rule.DatedTo || !ParticipationPath.ProjectedPensionAgeYears.TryGetValue(id, out int[] years)) { return statute; }
            float[] ages = ParticipationPath.ProjectedPensionAge[id];
            double projected = ages[ages.Length - 1];
            if (year <= years[0]) { projected = ages[0]; }
            else
            {
                for (int k = 1; k < years.Length; k++)
                {
                    if (year > years[k]) { continue; }
                    double t = (double)(year - years[k - 1]) / (years[k] - years[k - 1]);
                    projected = ages[k - 1] + (ages[k] - (double)ages[k - 1]) * t;
                    break;
                }
            }
            return Math.Max(statute, projected);
        }

        /// <summary>This file's own response, points of the 15+ rate, from the age <paramref name="from"/> to the age <paramref name="to"/>: Σ band × the share
        /// of the band between the two ages × the step, capped at the band's room, over the 15+ population, signed (to - from); <paramref name="older"/> the
        /// same over the bands at 55 and over only. Zero where the two ages agree.</summary>
        private static double ExpectedPoints(Country c, int year, double from, double to, out double older)
        {
            float[] rates = ParticipationRateTable.RatesAt(c.Id, year);
            float[] counts = c.Cohorts.Counts;
            older = 0.0;
            if (Math.Abs(to - from) < 1e-4) { return 0.0; }
            double lower = Math.Min(from, to), upper = Math.Max(from, to), sign = to > from ? 1.0 : -1.0;
            double step = PensionParticipationResponse.TryMeasured(c.Id, out float measured) ? measured : RateAt(rates, lower - 1.0) * 0.425;
            double extra = 0, extraOlder = 0, base15 = 0;
            for (int b = 3; b < PopulationCohorts.CohortCount; b++)
            {
                base15 += counts[b];
                if (b == PopulationCohorts.OpenBandIndex) { continue; }
                double start = b * 5.0, end = start + 5.0;
                double overlap = Math.Min(end, upper) - Math.Max(start, lower);
                if (overlap <= 0) { continue; }
                double room = sign > 0 ? 1.0 - rates[b] : rates[b];
                double e = sign * counts[b] * (overlap / 5.0) * Math.Min(step, Math.Max(0.0, room));
                extra += e;
                if (start >= 55.0) { extraOlder += e; }
            }
            older = base15 > 0 ? 100.0 * extraOlder / base15 : 0.0;
            return base15 > 0 ? 100.0 * extra / base15 : 0.0;
        }

        /// <summary>The rate at a single year of age, linear between the bands' midpoints, flat beyond the first and last - recomputed here.</summary>
        private static double RateAt(float[] rates, double age)
        {
            double pos = (age - 2.5) / 5.0;
            int n = Math.Min(rates.Length, PopulationCohorts.CohortCount);
            if (pos <= 0) { return rates[0]; }
            if (pos >= n - 1) { return rates[n - 1]; }
            int b = (int)Math.Floor(pos);
            return rates[b] + (rates[b + 1] - rates[b]) * (pos - b);
        }

        // ============================================================ (c) the labour force against the sources, the no-policy run
        private static void LabourForce()
        {
            _sb.Append(F("    c. the labour force against the sources, the no-policy run (an index on the run's first year the source covers; band +/-{0:P0})\n", LabourForceBand));
            foreach (CountryId id in Six)
            {
                IReadOnlyList<NoPolicyCentury.Year> run = NoPolicyCentury.For(id);
                var lf = new Dictionary<int, double>(); var lf2064 = new Dictionary<int, double>(); var lf2074 = new Dictionary<int, double>(); var part = new Dictionary<int, double>(); var structural = new Dictionary<int, double>(); var pop15 = new Dictionary<int, double>(); var terms = new Dictionary<int, NoPolicyCentury.Year>();
                foreach (NoPolicyCentury.Year r in run)
                {
                    // K299 (review M2, K299's prereg amendment r2): a record is keyed by the year its pyramid stands at, as (d) keys it. The floored
                    // mid-year of its span, the key before, trails the pyramid by a year for a run that opens in the first half of its year (the USA's:
                    // its "2040 on 2025" read the pyramid's 2041 on 2026) and equals it for a run that opens in the second half
                    int y = r.SubstrateYear;
                    if (!lf.ContainsKey(y)) { lf[y] = r.LabourForce; lf2064[y] = r.LabourForce2064; lf2074[y] = r.LabourForce2074; part[y] = r.Participation; structural[y] = r.Structural; pop15[y] = r.Population15; terms[y] = r; }
                }
                bool usa = id == CountryId.USA;
                int srcFirst = usa ? LongRunAnchors.PotentialGrowthFirstYear[id] : ParticipationPath.EuFirstYear;
                int baseYear = int.MaxValue;
                foreach (int y in lf.Keys) { if (y >= srcFirst && y < baseYear) { baseYear = y; } }
                if (!Check(baseYear != int.MaxValue, F("(c) {0,-8} the run covers a year of the source", id))) { continue; }
                int held = 0;
                foreach (int y in usa ? UsLabourYears : EuYears)
                {
                    if (!lf.ContainsKey(y)) { continue; }
                    held++;
                    double model, source;
                    if (usa)
                    {
                        model = lf[y] / lf[baseYear];
                        source = 1.0;
                        float[] g = LongRunAnchors.LabourGrowth[id];
                        for (int t = baseYear + 1; t <= y; t++) { source *= 1.0 + g[t - srcFirst] / 100.0; }
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        // review 1 (M2, the prereg's r2-3): the model's own labour force aged 20-74 against the Ageing Report's, employment / (1 - the rate)
                        model = lf2074[y] / lf2074[baseYear];
                        source = Lf2074(id, y) / Lf2074(id, baseYear);
                        float[] s = ParticipationPath.LabourForce2064[id];
                        double info2064 = (lf2064[y] / lf2064[baseYear]) / ((double)s[y - srcFirst] / s[baseYear - srcFirst]) - 1.0;
                        _sb.Append(F("        info (c) {0,-8} {1}: the 20-64 construct at the year's rates against II.1.26 {2:+0.00%;-0.00%} (information, review 1's M2)\n", id, y, info2064));
                    }
                    // review 1 (M2, M3): the attribution, information (and for the USA K290's registration condition) - the 15+ labour force is the 15+ population x the anchor x (the state's rate / the
                    // anchor); for the USA beside CBO's own: its labour force index over its all-people (16+) rate index is the population CBO's rate applies to
                    double popIx = pop15[y] / pop15[baseYear], anchorIx = structural[y] / structural[baseYear];
                    double kNow = part[y] / structural[y], kBase = part[baseYear] / structural[baseYear];
                    string cbo = string.Empty;
                    double popPart = double.NaN, ratePart = double.NaN;   // K290: the miss split (the USA only)
                    if (usa)
                    {
                        double rateIx = (double)ParticipationPath.UsAll16Plus[Math.Min(ParticipationPath.UsAll16Plus.Length - 1, y - ParticipationPath.UsFirstYear)]
                                        / ParticipationPath.UsAll16Plus[Math.Max(0, baseYear - ParticipationPath.UsFirstYear)];
                        cbo = F("; CBO: its all-people (16+, actual) rate x{0:F4}, so the population its rate applies to x{1:F4} (the potential rate is not in the file)", rateIx, source / rateIx);
                        // K290: the miss split exactly - model / source = (the model's rate index / CBO's) x (the 15+ population index / CBO's implied population's)
                        ratePart = (lf[y] / pop15[y]) / (lf[baseYear] / pop15[baseYear]) / rateIx - 1.0; popPart = popIx / (source / rateIx) - 1.0;
                        cbo += F("; the miss split: the rate part {0:+0.00%;-0.00%}, the population part {1:+0.00%;-0.00%}", ratePart, popPart);
                        // K299 (information): the same miss split against CBO's ACTUAL labour force - its civilian noninstitutionalized 16+ (Figure 10, the
                        // LTBO's actual labour force over its actual rate) x that rate - exactly: model / source = (1 + the rate part) x (the 15+ index / the
                        // civilian 16+'s) x (CBO's actual labour force / its potential); the last term is CBO's potential labour force converging on its actual
                        double civIx = (double)UsCivilian16(y) / UsCivilian16(baseYear), actualIx = civIx * rateIx;
                        cbo += F("; against CBO's actual labour force (K299): the population part against its civilian 16+ x{0:F4} {1:+0.00%;-0.00%}, its actual labour force over its potential {2:+0.00%;-0.00%}",
                            civIx, popIx / civIx - 1.0, actualIx / source - 1.0);
                    }
                    _sb.Append(F("        info (c) {0,-8} {1}: the 15+ population x{2:F4}; the anchor (structural, with the response) x{3:F4}, {4:F2} % against {5:F2} %; the state's rate over the anchor {6:F4} against {7:F4} at {8}{9}\n",
                        id, y, popIx, anchorIx, structural[y], structural[baseYear], kNow, kBase, baseYear, cbo));
                    // K313: the line with the health and education terms taken off the state's rate, at the year and at the base year (the participation route; the
                    // mortality route through the 15+ population stays in it), and their part - the line less that line. The EU lines only (the USA's split is K290's).
                    double withoutHe = double.NaN, hePart = double.NaN;
                    if (!usa && part[y] > 0.0 && part[baseYear] > 0.0)
                    {
                        double heNow = terms[y].HealthTerm + terms[y].EducationTerm, heBase = terms[baseYear].HealthTerm + terms[baseYear].EducationTerm;
                        withoutHe = (lf2074[y] * (part[y] - heNow) / part[y]) / (lf2074[baseYear] * (part[baseYear] - heBase) / part[baseYear]) / source - 1.0;
                        hePart = (model / source - 1.0) - withoutHe;
                        _sb.Append(F("        info (c) {0,-8} {1}: without the health and education terms (their {2:+0.00;-0.00} pts at the year, {3:+0.00;-0.00} at {4}) the line reads {5:+0.00%;-0.00%}; their part {6:+0.00%;-0.00%} (K313)\n",
                            id, y, heNow, heBase, baseYear, withoutHe, hePart));
                    }
                    _sb.Append(F("        info (c) {0,-8} {1}: what holds the state's rate off the anchor - unemployment {2:+0.00;-0.00} pts off the effective natural rate (the discouraged-worker term), the labour tax's term {3:+0.00;-0.00}, the health's {4:+0.00;-0.00}, the education's {5:+0.00;-0.00} pts\n",
                        id, y, terms[y].UnemploymentGap, terms[y].LabourTaxTerm, terms[y].HealthTerm, terms[y].EducationTerm));
                    Band(F("{0} {1}", id, y), popPart, ratePart, withoutHe, hePart, Math.Abs(model / source - 1.0) <= LabourForceBand,
                        F("(c) {0,-8} {1}: the labour force {2} at {3:F4} of {4} against {5}'s {6:F4} ({7:+0.00%;-0.00%}); participation {8:F2} % (15+, the state's), the 15+ labour force x{9:F4}",
                            id, y, usa ? "(15+, the state's rate)" : "aged 20-74 (the state's, on the source's law)", model, baseYear, usa ? "CBO's potential labor force" : "the Ageing Report's 20-74 (II.1.53 / (1 - II.1.51))", source, model / source - 1.0, part[y], lf[y] / lf[baseYear]));
                }
                Check(held > 0, F("(c) {0,-8} {1} stated year(s) inside the run - none is a check that did not run", id, held));
            }
        }

        // ============================================================ (d) K299: the USA's population against CBO's 2025 demographics, the no-policy run
        /// <summary>K299 (K290's follow-up): the USA's no-policy pyramid against CBO's 2025 demographics (UsDemographicOutlook, Tools/uspop_prep.pl), by
        /// the pyramid's own year (NoPolicyCentury.Year.SubstrateYear: the year the boundary's commit stepped it to), as an index on
        /// <see cref="UsPopulationBase"/>, at <see cref="UsPopulationYears"/>: (d1) every Figure 2 group and the sum from 25 within <see cref="UsGroupBand"/>
        /// of CBO's own index, the whole population printed against Figure 2's total; (d2) the 16+ within <see cref="UsCivilianBand"/> of CBO's civilian
        /// noninstitutionalized 16+ (Figure 10, the population CBO's labour-force rate applies to); (d3) the 15+ and the 16+ within <see cref="UsAdultBand"/>
        /// of CBO's own Social Security area 15+ and 16+ (the by-age table's single years). The bands and years are K299's prereg and its amendment r3
        /// (Reviews/2026-10-29_uspop_prereg.md), DECLARED before any run of the tree they govern.</summary>
        private static void Population()
        {
            _sb.Append(F("    d. K299: the USA's population against CBO's 2025 demographics, the no-policy run, by the pyramid's own year (an index on {0}; the groups +/-{1:P1}, the 16+ against CBO's civilian 16+ +/-{2:P1}, the 15+ and 16+ against CBO's own +/-{3:P1})\n",
                UsPopulationBase, UsGroupBand, UsCivilianBand, UsAdultBand));
            var byYear = new Dictionary<int, float[]>();
            foreach (NoPolicyCentury.Year r in NoPolicyCentury.For(CountryId.USA))
            {
                if (r.Pyramid != null && !byYear.ContainsKey(r.SubstrateYear)) { byYear[r.SubstrateYear] = r.Pyramid; }
            }
            if (!Check(byYear.ContainsKey(UsPopulationBase), F("(d) USA      the run's pyramid stands at {0}, the base", UsPopulationBase))) { return; }
            float[] p0 = byYear[UsPopulationBase];
            int from = UsDemographicOutlook.GroupAges[1][0];   // the sum from CBO's second group (25)
            int held = 0;
            foreach (int y in UsPopulationYears)
            {
                if (!byYear.ContainsKey(y)) { continue; }
                held++;
                float[] p = byYear[y];
                double modelAll = 0, cboAll = 0, modelAll0 = 0, cboAll0 = 0;
                for (int g = 0; g < UsDemographicOutlook.GroupAges.Length; g++)
                {
                    int lo = UsDemographicOutlook.GroupAges[g][0], hi = UsDemographicOutlook.GroupAges[g][1];
                    double m = Bands(p, lo, hi), m0 = Bands(p0, lo, hi), c = UsDemographicOutlook.Group(g, y), c0 = UsDemographicOutlook.Group(g, UsPopulationBase);
                    double model = m / m0, cbo = c / c0;
                    Check(Math.Abs(model / cbo - 1.0) <= UsGroupBand, F("(d1) USA      {0}: ages {1} at x{2:F4} of {3} against CBO's Figure 2 x{4:F4} ({5:+0.00%;-0.00%})",
                        y, hi >= 999 ? lo + "+" : lo + "-" + hi, model, UsPopulationBase, cbo, model / cbo - 1.0));
                    if (lo < from) { continue; }
                    modelAll += m; modelAll0 += m0; cboAll += c; cboAll0 += c0;
                }
                Check(Math.Abs((modelAll / modelAll0) / (cboAll / cboAll0) - 1.0) <= UsGroupBand, F("(d1) USA      {0}: ages {1}+ at x{2:F4} of {3} against CBO's Figure 2 x{4:F4} ({5:+0.00%;-0.00%})",
                    y, from, modelAll / modelAll0, UsPopulationBase, cboAll / cboAll0, (modelAll / modelAll0) / (cboAll / cboAll0) - 1.0));
                // review L4 (information): the whole population against CBO's total
                double total = Bands(p, 0, 999) / Bands(p0, 0, 999), cboTotal = (double)UsTotal(y) / UsTotal(UsPopulationBase);
                _sb.Append(F("        info (d1) USA      {0}: the whole population at x{1:F4} of {2} against CBO's total (Figure 2) x{3:F4} ({4:+0.00%;-0.00%})\n", y, total, UsPopulationBase, cboTotal, total / cboTotal - 1.0));
                // (d2) the 16+: the bands from 20 and four fifths of 15-19 (uniform inside the band, DECLARED), against CBO's civilian noninstitutionalized 16+
                double m16 = (Bands(p, 20, 999) + 0.8 * p[3]) / (Bands(p0, 20, 999) + 0.8 * p0[3]);
                double m15 = Bands(p, 15, 999) / Bands(p0, 15, 999);
                double civ = (double)UsCivilian16(y) / UsCivilian16(UsPopulationBase);
                Check(Math.Abs(m16 / civ - 1.0) <= UsCivilianBand, F("(d2) USA      {0}: the 16+ at x{1:F4} of {2} against CBO's civilian noninstitutionalized 16+ (Figure 10) x{3:F4} ({4:+0.00%;-0.00%}); the 15+ x{5:F4} ({6:+0.00%;-0.00%})",
                    y, m16, UsPopulationBase, civ, m16 / civ - 1.0, m15, m15 / civ - 1.0));
                // (d3) amendment r3: the 15+ and the 16+ against CBO's own Social Security area 15+ and 16+, from the by-age table's single years
                double c15 = (double)UsAdult(UsDemographicOutlook.Population15Plus, y) / UsAdult(UsDemographicOutlook.Population15Plus, UsPopulationBase);
                double c16 = (double)UsAdult(UsDemographicOutlook.Population16Plus, y) / UsAdult(UsDemographicOutlook.Population16Plus, UsPopulationBase);
                Check(Math.Abs(m15 / c15 - 1.0) <= UsAdultBand, F("(d3) USA      {0}: the 15+ at x{1:F4} of {2} against CBO's own 15+ (the by-age table) x{3:F4} ({4:+0.00%;-0.00%})", y, m15, UsPopulationBase, c15, m15 / c15 - 1.0));
                Check(Math.Abs(m16 / c16 - 1.0) <= UsAdultBand, F("(d3) USA      {0}: the 16+ at x{1:F4} of {2} against CBO's own 16+ (the by-age table) x{3:F4} ({4:+0.00%;-0.00%})", y, m16, UsPopulationBase, c16, m16 / c16 - 1.0));
            }
            Check(held == UsPopulationYears.Length, F("(d) USA      {0} of the {1} stated years inside the run - none is a check that did not run", held, UsPopulationYears.Length));
        }

        /// <summary>K299: the stated years and the base of (d) - the years (c) holds the USA at, and (c)'s base, CBO's LTBO's first year.</summary>
        private static readonly int[] UsPopulationYears = { 2030, 2040, 2055 };
        private const int UsPopulationBase = 2025;

        /// <summary>[AUTHORED] K299's prereg: a Figure 2 group's index against CBO's, a share - DECLARED before any run of K299's tree.</summary>
        private const double UsGroupBand = 0.01;

        /// <summary>[AUTHORED] K299's prereg: the 16+ index against CBO's civilian noninstitutionalized 16+, a share - DECLARED before any run of K299's tree.</summary>
        private const double UsCivilianBand = 0.015;

        /// <summary>[AUTHORED] K299's prereg amendment r3: the 15+ and 16+ indices against CBO's own, a share - DECLARED before the code that reads it.</summary>
        private const double UsAdultBand = 0.01;

        private static float UsTotal(int year) => UsDemographicOutlook.Total[Math.Max(0, Math.Min(UsDemographicOutlook.LastYear - UsDemographicOutlook.FirstYear, year - UsDemographicOutlook.FirstYear))];

        private static float UsCivilian16(int year) => UsDemographicOutlook.Civilian16Plus[Math.Max(0, Math.Min(UsDemographicOutlook.LastYear - UsDemographicOutlook.FirstYear, year - UsDemographicOutlook.FirstYear))];

        private static float UsAdult(float[] series, int year) => series[Math.Max(0, Math.Min(UsDemographicOutlook.BandsLastYear - UsDemographicOutlook.BandsFirstYear, year - UsDemographicOutlook.BandsFirstYear))];

        /// <summary>A pyramid's millions over the bands from <paramref name="lo"/> to <paramref name="hi"/> (999: the open band), whole bands.</summary>
        private static double Bands(float[] p, int lo, int hi)
        {
            double s = 0;
            for (int b = lo / PopulationCohorts.CohortWidth; b < PopulationCohorts.CohortCount && b * PopulationCohorts.CohortWidth <= hi; b++) { s += p[b]; }
            return s;
        }

        /// <summary>The Ageing Report's labour force aged 20-74 in a year, millions: table II.1.53's employment / (1 - table II.1.51's unemployment rate / 100).</summary>
        private static double Lf2074(CountryId id, int year)
        {
            int i = year - ParticipationPath.EuFirstYear;
            return ParticipationPath.Employment2074[id][i] / (1.0 - ParticipationPath.Unemployment2074[id][i] / 100.0);
        }

        private static bool Check(bool ok, string what)
        {
            _sb.Append(ok ? "        ok   " : "        FAIL ").Append(what).Append('\n');
            if (!ok) { _failures++; Debug.LogError("PARTICIPATION COHORTS: FAIL - " + what); }
            return ok;
        }

        /// <summary>K290: a (c) line is asserted (<see cref="Check"/>) unless it is in <see cref="RegisteredLabourForce"/> AND its attribution holds, where a
        /// miss prints a named REGISTERED MISS with its attribution and does not fail; a registered line that holds says so, so the registration can be lifted.</summary>
        private static void Band(string key, double popPart, double ratePart, double withoutHe, double hePart, bool ok, string what)
        {
            if (!RegisteredLabourForce.TryGetValue(key, out (string Tag, string Reason, Attribution Kind, double MeasuredPopulationPart) reg)) { Check(ok, what); return; }
            string reason = reg.Reason;
            bool attributionHolds;
            string attribution;
            if (reg.Kind == Attribution.PopulationPart)
            {
                // review 3 (L1): the population part within the tolerance of the part measured at registration (a ceiling and a floor), the rate part inside the band
                attributionHolds = Math.Abs(popPart - reg.MeasuredPopulationPart) <= RegisteredPopulationTolerance && Math.Abs(ratePart) <= LabourForceBand;
                attribution = F("the population part {0:+0.00%;-0.00%} against the {1:+0.00%;-0.00%} measured at registration (+/-{2:P0}), the rate part {3:+0.00%;-0.00%} (band +/-{4:P0})", popPart, reg.MeasuredPopulationPart, RegisteredPopulationTolerance, ratePart, LabourForceBand);
            }
            else
            {
                // K313: the line without the health and education terms inside the band, and their part at most the bound
                attributionHolds = !double.IsNaN(withoutHe) && Math.Abs(withoutHe) <= LabourForceBand && Math.Abs(hePart) <= RegisteredHealthEducationPartBound;
                attribution = F("without the health and education terms the line reads {0:+0.00%;-0.00%} (band +/-{1:P0}), their part {2:+0.00%;-0.00%} (at most {3:P0}); the mortality route through the 15+ population is not separable and stays in the line without them", withoutHe, LabourForceBand, hePart, RegisteredHealthEducationPartBound);
            }
            if (ok) { _sb.Append("        ok   ").Append(what).Append(" - REGISTERED under ").Append(reg.Tag).Append(" and holding: the registration can be lifted\n"); return; }
            if (!attributionHolds) { Check(false, what + " - REGISTERED under " + reg.Tag + ", but its attribution no longer holds: " + attribution); return; }
            _sb.Append("        REGISTERED MISS (").Append(reg.Tag).Append(") ").Append(what).Append(" - ").Append(reason).Append(" - ").Append(attribution).Append('\n');
            _registered++;
            Debug.Log("PARTICIPATION COHORTS: REGISTERED MISS (" + reg.Tag + ") - " + what + " - " + reason + " - " + attribution);
        }

        private static string F(string format, params object[] args) => string.Format(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, format, args);
    }
}
